"""Colour by number on paintings, made for an older player.

A picture is a grid of cells, each with a number; the palette at the
bottom has one big button per number. Pick a colour, tap its cells.
- Cells of the chosen number are tinted and their numbers bold, so they
  are easy to find; a cell of another number cannot be painted.
- The buttons on the right carry drawn icons, no words: back, zoom in,
  zoom out (down to the whole picture on screen), "where?" (shows the
  nearest unpainted cell of the chosen colour), undo, full screen, and
  "look" (the finished picture while held). Drag to scroll.
- A tap paints the whole connected area of that number at once (a
  large sky is one tap).
- Every tap gives a short buzz; there is no timer, no score, no ads.
- Progress is saved after every tap, so a picture can wait for tomorrow;
  the program starts on the last picture, unless it is finished, and the
  gallery opens at that picture's card.

The gallery runs from easier to harder as it scrolls down: paintings in
64 cells along the long side with up to 16 colours, then in 96 cells
with up to 24 colours.

Pictures: the built-in ones in /usr/local/share/b8k/paint/, and any photo
put into ~/Раскраски (JPEG or PNG), which is turned into a picture of 64
cells along the long side and up to 16 colours the first time it is shown.
"""
